## Modifications in this fork

1. Added `src/search.ts` and the `session_search_global` tool: full-text search
   over the host `sessionQuery` corpus across **all workspaces**, with a bounded
   fallback scan when the optional full-text index is closed.
2. Added the `readOnlyTools` plugin config field. When true, only read-only
   tools register (`session_search_global`, `session_bridge_find`,
   `session_bridge_read`, `session_bridge_segments`, `session_bridge_status`);
   create/send/wait/resume/cancel/monitor/archive tools are not exposed.
   This checkout's bundle row sets `readOnlyTools: false` (all tools); set it to
   `true` to expose only the read-only subset. The value is read when the row is
   (re)loaded, so changing it needs a full DSH restart.
3. Updated package metadata, `dsh.plugin.json`, READMEs, and this NOTICE for the
   fork. The upstream tool behavior is otherwise unchanged.
4. Enabled the host full-text index from this bundle's patch layer: the
   `session-query-sqlite` row now uses `path: dshHomePath('session-search.db')`
   and `openAt: first-search` (upstream documents this override for deployments
   that want content search). This makes `session_search_global` index-backed;
   the DB rebuilds when deleted. Changing this row requires a full DSH restart —
   hot-toggling a bundle whose patch touches the core `sessionQuery` service can
   stall the host during unload (one such incident happened during development;
   a full restart recovered it with no config or code damage).

